# MKTEMP(3)

## NAME

mktemp - make a unique file name

## SYNOPSIS

```c
char *mktemp(char *template);
```

## DESCRIPTION

*Mktemp* replaces *template* by a unique file name, and returns the address of the template.
The template should look like a file name with six trailing X's, which will be replaced with
the current process id and a unique letter.

**Note:** v7 declared it in no header and C11 has no such routine, so every v7 caller declared
it itself. This port declares it in *<stdio.h>*, beside *tmpnam*, because the strict front end
takes no undeclared call.

## SEE ALSO

mkstemp(3), getpid(2), fopen(3) for *tmpnam*

## FILES

| share/besm6/lib/libc.a
| lib/libc/gen/mktemp.c

## BUGS

**It walks a single letter,** so it can distinguish 26 names for a given process and no more.
That is why tmpnam(3) does *not* call it: TMP_MAX promises 26**3, and *tmpnam* counts three
letters of its own.
